# Trivy ignore list — every entry here is a scoped, dated exception, not a
# blanket severity downgrade (SPRINT_0_PLAN §21 "known-gaps register, not a
# confession" culture, Blueprint §10.6). New vulnerabilities in any package,
# including perl-base, still fail the build; only the exact CVE IDs below
# are suppressed, and only until Debian ships a fix.
#
# All four CVEs below are in perl-base, a component of the upstream
# python:3.12-slim (Debian trixie) base image — Aether's API/worker never
# invokes perl. perl-base is an Essential Debian package
# (`apt-get remove` refuses without --allow-remove-essential); force-removing
# an Essential package from a base image is out of scope for a Sprint 0
# hardening pass. No fixed version is published upstream for any of these
# as of 2026-08-14 (checked via `trivy image` Fixed-Version column).
# Tracked: https://github.com/Sudeepxe/aether-ai-workspace/issues/2
# Revisit: when Debian trixie ships a patched perl-base, or when this image
# is replaced by a perl-free base (also tracked in issue #2).
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-8376

# CVE-2026-56854 is a CRITICAL SSH server-side auth-bypass in
# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh@v0.52.0 (fixed 0.55.0), flagged as a gobinary
# finding against usr/bin/caddy in the pinned caddy:2-alpine base image
# used by infra/docker/web.Dockerfile (aether-web:ci scan only — the
# aether-api:ci image doesn't contain this binary).
#
# Reachability was checked, not assumed, before accepting this risk:
#   - `govulncheck -mode=binary` against the real extracted caddy binary
#     (pulled at the exact pinned digest) confirms the vulnerable
#     ssh.NewServerConn symbol IS compiled in — it's a transitive
#     dependency of Caddy's built-in `pki` app (github.com/smallstep/
#     certificates, step-ca's SSH CA support), not something Caddy
#     itself exposes.
#   - `caddy list-modules` on that same binary lists all 134 compiled-in
#     Caddy modules: none contain "ssh". Caddy's own config schema
#     (Caddyfile or JSON) has no module that can start an SSH server —
#     there is no config-reachable way to activate this code path.
#   - `caddy help` lists every CLI subcommand: no SSH-related subcommand
#     exists either.
#   - This deployment uses the image's own default Caddyfile (no custom
#     config is supplied — see web.Dockerfile), which only enables
#     `file_server` on `:80`. web.Dockerfile EXPOSEs port 80 only; the
#     image itself declares 80/443/2019 (admin API), never 22.
# Net: the vulnerable function is present in the binary but dead code
# from every actual entrypoint this deployment uses — no config, CLI
# invocation, or listening port reaches it.
# No patched tag exists yet (checked 2026-09-04): caddy:2-alpine,
# caddy:latest, and caddy:2 are all byte-identical to the pinned digest;
# caddy:2.10-alpine is strictly worse (same unfixed CVE plus additional
# CRITICALs in its bundled Go binaries).
# Tracked: https://github.com/Sudeepxe/aether-ai-workspace/issues/136
# Revisit: bump the caddy:2-alpine pin as soon as an upstream image
# ships golang.org/x/crypto >= 0.55.0, or immediately if Aether ever
# gains a feature that runs an actual SSH server in this image (also
# tracked in issue #136).
CVE-2026-56854
